  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Leave the EU to restore full sovereignty; protect British common law; more police with deterrent sentencing and “life means life”; skills‑based immigration with faster, secure asylum processing; NHS +£2bn and higher nurse pay; small tax cuts for the low paid; defence spending rise. TEXT_G: Free personal care for the elderly; recruit 1,500 nurses, halve inpatient waiting times, free dental check‑ups and healthier school meals; abolish tuition fees and reduce early‑years class sizes; anti‑poverty strategy and end asylum vouchers with fast, fair assessment; raise the minimum wage and strengthen trade union rights; 1,000 more police, tougher on dealers, speed up courts, lifelong supervision for high‑risk sex offenders; proportional representation and inclusive citizenship; progressive tax measure (5p band over £100k) while reviewing for fairness and simplicity.",
  "reasoning": "Given the electorate’s priorities (Care and Authority highest, then Equality and Proportionality), TEXT_G places stronger emphasis on concrete care and equality measures while maintaining authority through policing and justice reforms. TEXT_C leans more on loyalty/sovereignty and stricter law‑and‑order than on care/equality, making it a weaker fit to the stated profile.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_G"
